{
  "id": "kerbalism-elected",
  "name": "Kerbalism elected, modelling reliability",
  "description": "Kerbalism's reliability feature is ON and it won the election, which is stock-Kerbalism's normal state. It exists because without it the Kerbalism half of the model is never rendered by any test at all: kerbalism-elected-off's blank comes from an empty part list, not from a widget gate, so a Kerbalism craft with a failed part was a state no render could reach. Kerbalism publishes conditions and a service clock and no probability of any kind, so the rows here carry no survival figure, which is the visible difference from the TestFlight install.",
